Source: @SOURCE@
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake (>= 3.16),
               libpio-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/fpgas-online/fpgas.online-fpga-tools
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/fpgas-online/fpgas.online-fpga-tools.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/fpgas-online/fpgas.online-fpga-tools

Package: librp1jtag0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: JTAG through the Raspberry Pi 5 RP1 PIO block (shared library)
 librp1jtag shifts JTAG through the RP1 PIO block of the Raspberry Pi 5
 instead of bit-banging PCIe-attached GPIOs. openfpgaloader-fpgasonline
 (the rp1pio cable) and openocd-fpgasonline (the rp1_pio_jtag adapter) use
 it. This is the fpgas.online build of @UPSTREAM_URL@
 @UPSTREAM_REF@ (commit @UPSTREAM_COMMIT@).
 .
 It exports the rp1_jtag_* API only, and reaches /dev/pio0 through the
 system PIOLib (libpio0) rather than a private copy of it.

Package: librp1jtag-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: librp1jtag0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: JTAG through the Raspberry Pi 5 RP1 PIO block (development files)
 librp1jtag shifts JTAG through the RP1 PIO block of the Raspberry Pi 5.
 .
 This package contains the header, the linker symlink and the pkg-config
 file (rp1jtag.pc) needed to build against librp1jtag0.
